# src/core stack-frame caps in bytes (name<TAB>cap).
# Generated from the xmppd-core Debug build on freebsd-dev1 at the
# v091/measure-m4 merge of master 8086a6a (Zig emits __zig_probe_stack;
# caps record the probe immediate). A function fails the check when its
# frame exceeds its cap or has no cap at all; lower caps as frames shrink.
# Symbol names re-keyed to the ADR-12 layout (C7); caps unchanged.
#
# Re-measured at 941c1db (CI-QUALITY) on a -Dcpu=baseline build, matching the
# quality job: native codegen differs by a few bytes between hosts (dev1 vs
# runner01 moved five rows by up to 72 B and hid a +16 B Session.init), so the
# job pins baseline to keep caps host-independent. The job died at the dane-zig
# dependency fetch on every run since 2616, so reviewed merges grew these
# frames without the ratchet ever firing. Each raised cap is intentional
# work, not an accident:
#   main.main      +32 M1 merge a56c464 (363da75 metrics init), then
#                  +224 A2 merge ca38cb6 (61e8fcf FrameReader/Writer types)
#   main.workerThread +64 A2 merge ca38cb6 (61e8fcf)
#   worker.Server.run +448 M1 merge a56c464 (363da75 iter_timer + dump args)
#   worker.Server.initFromFdOpts +192 A2 merge ca38cb6 (61e8fcf)
#   worker.Server.initWithMaxSessions +224 A2 merge ca38cb6 (61e8fcf)
#   muc.handler.handleMucDiscoItems +608 R4R5 merge a9074b4 (8b91874 zero
#                  silent drops rework: dir_entries[256] + reply builders)
#   muc.handler.handleMucGroupchat +32 2e67b8b (S32 mints a stanza id into
#                  sid_buf[32] for id-less groupchat), +32 8b91874 (R5)
#   C2 merge: Connection's 16 KiB outbox ring backing moved to a lazy heap
#     block (ensureWriteBuf), so by-value Connection frames shrank ~16 KiB
#     per slot and Session.init fell under the 16 KiB threshold entirely;
#     its row is removed so any return is flagged as new.
#   c2s.session.Session.init +16: not a code change; codegen only. A
#     -Dcpu=baseline build at the original measurement point 8086a6a
#     already probes 0x7B30 (31536) where the native build probes 0x7B20
#     (31520); the init body and every input type (Session, Connection,
#     xml.Reader, xmpp.Stream) are identical across the window, so no
#     commit in the range grew the frame. The +16 records the
#     -Dcpu=baseline measurement pin itself.
#   main.main      +192 Q1 203a49b (pre-rebase fc7d7de): Root.init union
#                  wraps the DebugAllocator in Debug builds (-Dallocator
#                  default debug)
